  "notes": "Official cause code B (Design/Manufacturing/Installation) governs category despite substantial procedural/personnel-failure narrative content; theme captures both drift-design and missed-evaluation angles. Two physical transmitter units (S/N 452 removed April 2025, S/N 449 removed Nov 2025) occupied the 1-PT-0458 location across the three inoperability windows; both modeled as one Component node representing the tag/location per narrative's continuous treatment of '1-PT-0458' as the failing channel. Previous similar events are CAP condition reports (CR-/TR- prefixed), not NRC LERs, but modeled as stub LER nodes per rule 9 since they are the referenced 'previous similar occurrence' records; their stub keys are copied verbatim as stated (CR-/TR- numbers) rather than invented docket-based LER numbers. RTS/ESFAS design-context systems (solid state protection system, reactor trip switchgear) not modeled since narrative describes them only for architecture/context, not as involved/backup components."
